<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="A sanitized home-server infrastructure case study."><title>Backups · Home Server</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"></head><body><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="../index.html" aria-label="Engineering Notebook home"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h6v6H4zM14 4h6v6h-6zM4 14h6v6H4zM14 14h6v6h-6z"/></svg><span class="nav-label">Engineering Notebook</span></a><nav aria-label="Home-server navigation"><div class="home-server-links"><a href="/home-server/">Overview</a><a href="/home-server/hardware/">Hardware</a><a href="/home-server/security/">Security</a><a href="/home-server/monitoring/">Monitoring</a><a class="active" href="/home-server/backups/">Backups</a><a href="/home-server/services/">Services</a><a href="/home-server/lessons/">Lessons</a></div><a href="/projects/"><span class="nav-label">← Projects</span></a></nav></header><main><section class="intro section-shell"><p class="eyebrow">HOME SERVER / BACKUPS</p><h1>Backups</h1><p class="lede">A backup is not a comforting file name. It is a file that can be decrypted and restored when the original machine is unavailable.</p><button class="intro-scroll-cue" type="button" aria-label="Scroll to next section"></button></section><section class="section-shell"><div class="feature-card"><div class="card-kicker">RECOVERY</div><h3>Encryption made the backup safer and the passphrase more important.</h3><p>Configuration, monitoring files, and application data are packaged into archives and encrypted with age. Grafana and Prometheus data are included so dashboards, alerts, and historical observations can be recovered.</p><p>The first passphrase-based attempt taught an unfriendly lesson: a passphrase that was not recorded could not unlock the archive. A key-based backup was then created and restore-tested by extracting more than two thousand files into a temporary directory.</p></div></section><section class="section-shell"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">OPERATING MODEL</p><h2>The server can be off without losing the project.</h2></div><div class="note-grid"><article class="note-card"><span>01</span><h3>Separate storage</h3><p>Encrypted backups live on the Mac in the private homeserver workspace, separate from the running server.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>02</span><h3>Restore test</h3><p>Archives are checked by decrypting and extracting them, not by trusting that they were created successfully.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>03</span><h3>Future work</h3><p>Recurring backup automation and retention limits remain maintenance work before public launch.</p></article></div></section></main><script is:inline src="../../scroll-cue.js"></script></body></html>